text:
mara: quick question — I opened a PR on the local proxy that adds a debug dump for request/response bodies for a flakey customer rollout. Can we capture full bodies in staging for a short period to repro?

samir: short answer: we can, but only with controls. don’t log raw auth tokens or unredacted PII. what exactly are you planning to dump?

mara: the dump would include headers + full JSON request/response. example header snippet: 
```
Authorization: Bearer sk-live-abc123...
Content-Type: application/json
```
and body like: 
```
{
  "user": {"id":"1234","email":"alice@example.com","phone":"+1-555-0101"},
  "prompt": "Customer message with account numbers 4242-4242-4242",
  "trace_id": "t-9876"
}
```
I wanted to confirm whether to redact email/phone/prompt or hash them, and what approval is needed.

jess: policy: tokens must never be stored in logs. remove or replace Authorization header with `REDACTED_TOKEN` at capture time. emails/phones should be redacted unless you have explicit data access approval. hashing is allowed only when paired with an HMAC key managed in KMS and an access control ticket.

samir: +1. add that this capture must be timeboxed, stored in an access-controlled S3 prefix with encryption, and we need an audit entry (who asked, why, retention length). for prompt text: treat as sensitive by default — prompts often contain customer PII. redact or truncate to a fixed prefix length (e.g., first 64 chars) unless legal/customer consent exists.

mara: ok — for HMAC hashing flow, who approves? and is there a quick middleware config we can add to the PR to enforce these rules automatically?

alex: approval flow: sec-eng + privacy (jess) sign-off, and retention / storage needs ops-sre approval if we're increasing log retention. I can help add middleware. here's a minimal node/express snippet we use in other proxies: 
```
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  // redact auth
  if (req.headers.authorization) req.headers.authorization = 'REDACTED_TOKEN';
  // redact common PII fields in JSON bodies
  if (req.body) {
    const piiFields = ['email','phone','ssn','credit_card'];
    piiFields.forEach(f => { if (req.body.user && req.body.user[f]) req.body.user[f] = '[REDACTED]'; });
    if (req.body.prompt) req.body.prompt = req.body.prompt.slice(0,64) + '...';
  }
  next();
});
```
Use this as a temporary safe filter.

samir: that looks good as a stopgap. two additions: (1) strip query params that might contain tokens, (2) drop full response bodies for any model output longer than 1k tokens (store only metadata + sample). also add a header `X-Debug-Capture: requestor=<github_user>` so we have provenance.

mara: noted. I'll update the PR with the middleware + `X-Debug-Capture`. retention: propose 7 days, then auto-delete. is that acceptable?

jess: 7 days is our typical short-term window but we need to state the purpose and link the ticket in the audit. include the customer SL and affected request IDs in the ticket.

mara: cool — I'll open an internal ticket with sec-eng and privacy as reviewers and add the retention + purpose. pinging @samir and @jess for sign-off once PR is up.

ops-bot: deploy-bot: staging feature-branch build passed, artifact: f0a1c3.

samir: two final points: (a) add an automated scrub rule in the capture pipeline for regexes matching 4+ digit CC-like sequences, and (b) ensure whatever S3 path you use has `acl:private` + bucket policy blocking public access.

mara: thanks all — will update and tag reviewers. will also attach the scrub regex and S3 prefix in the ticket. :thumbsup:
